<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Prussian War</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Prussian War of 1870–1871 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and a German coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. The German victory led to the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>, the annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace-lorraine">Alsace-Lorraine</a> and the proclamation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> in January 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Prussian War" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton von Werner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_v_Werner_-_Kaiserproklamation_am_18_Januar_1871_(3._Fassung_1885).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
